<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <meta name="theme-color" content="#f4f2f8">
    <title>Queuezy Terms and Privacy Policy</title>
    <style>
        :root {
            color-scheme: light;
            font-family: Inter, "Segoe UI", sans-serif;
            color: #262238;
            background: #f4f2f8;
            font-synthesis: none;
            text-rendering: optimizeLegibility;
        }

        * { box-sizing: border-box; }

        body {
            min-width: 320px;
            margin: 0;
            background: #f4f2f8;
        }

        a { color: #6844c0; }

        .policy-shell {
            width: min(900px, calc(100% - 36px));
            margin: 0 auto;
            padding: 32px 0 56px;
        }

        .policy-topbar {
            display: flex;
            align-items: center;
            justify-content: space-between;
            gap: 20px;
            margin-bottom: 34px;
        }

        .brand {
            color: #28213f;
            font-size: 1.05rem;
            font-weight: 800;
            letter-spacing: 0.04em;
            text-decoration: none;
        }

        .back-link {
            font-size: 0.88rem;
            font-weight: 700;
            text-decoration-thickness: 1px;
            text-underline-offset: 3px;
        }

        .policy-header { margin-bottom: 28px; }

        .policy-header h1 {
            margin: 0;
            font-size: clamp(1.8rem, 5vw, 2.4rem);
            line-height: 1.15;
        }

        .policy-header p {
            margin: 10px 0 0;
            color: #625d70;
            font-size: 0.96rem;
            line-height: 1.6;
        }

        .policy-nav {
            display: flex;
            flex-wrap: wrap;
            gap: 18px;
            padding: 0 0 18px;
            border-bottom: 1px solid #dcd8e5;
            font-size: 0.9rem;
            font-weight: 700;
        }

        .policy-section {
            padding: 30px 0;
            border-bottom: 1px solid #dcd8e5;
            scroll-margin-top: 20px;
        }

        .policy-section h2 {
            margin: 0 0 18px;
            color: #30274b;
            font-size: 1.45rem;
        }

        .policy-section h3 {
            margin: 24px 0 8px;
            color: #30274b;
            font-size: 1rem;
        }

        .policy-section p,
        .policy-section li {
            color: #504b5e;
            font-size: 0.94rem;
            line-height: 1.75;
        }

        .policy-section p { margin: 0 0 12px; }
        .policy-section ul { margin: 8px 0 16px; padding-left: 22px; }

        .policy-updated {
            margin: 24px 0 0;
            color: #716b7e;
            font-size: 0.82rem;
        }

        @media (max-width: 520px) {
            .policy-shell { width: min(100% - 28px, 900px); padding-top: 22px; }
            .policy-topbar { margin-bottom: 28px; }
            .policy-section { padding: 24px 0; }
        }
    </style>
</head>
<body>
    <div class="policy-shell">
        <header class="policy-topbar">
            <span class="brand">QUEUEZY</span>
        </header>

        <main>
            <header class="policy-header">
                <h1>Queuezy policies</h1>
                <p>These policies explain the rules for using Queuezy and how information is handled when you create an account or use queue services.</p>
                <p class="policy-updated">Last updated: October 15, 2026</p>
            </header>

            <nav class="policy-nav" aria-label="Policy sections">
                <a href="#terms">Terms of Service</a>
                <a href="#privacy">Privacy Policy</a>
            </nav>

            <section class="policy-section" id="terms" aria-labelledby="terms-title">
                <h2 id="terms-title">Terms of Service</h2>
                <p>By creating a Queuezy account or using its queue services, you agree to these terms. If you do not agree, do not create an account or use the service.</p>

                <h3>Accounts and verification</h3>
                <p>Provide accurate registration details and keep your sign-in credentials private. Queuezy may require email verification before completing registration. You are responsible for activity performed through your account and should promptly report suspected unauthorized use to the service administrator.</p>

                <h3>Queue services</h3>
                <p>Queuezy provides queue tickets and status information for participating services. A ticket records your place and service selection, but estimated wait times are not guarantees. Follow instructions from authorized staff, and do not misuse or attempt to disrupt the queue or service.</p>

                <h3>Fees and payment records</h3>
                <p>Applicable service fees are shown in Queuezy before or during service. Queuezy may record a ticket's amount and payment status. Any separate payment method or provider is subject to its own terms.</p>

                <h3>Availability and changes</h3>
                <p>Queuezy may be unavailable or change as the service is maintained. Features, queue availability, and service details may be updated. We may restrict access where necessary to protect the service, its users, or its operation.</p>

                <h3>Contact</h3>
                <p>For account or service questions, contact the Queuezy administrator or the staff at the participating service.</p>
            </section>

            <section class="policy-section" id="privacy" aria-labelledby="privacy-title">
                <h2 id="privacy-title">Privacy Policy</h2>
                <p>This policy describes information handled by Queuezy's registration and queue features.</p>

                <h3>Information Queuezy handles</h3>
                <ul>
                    <li>Account details such as your name, email address, account role, and a securely hashed password.</li>
                    <li>Email verification and account-recovery information needed to confirm or protect your account.</li>
                    <li>Queue activity, including ticket number, selected service, status, timestamps, and related fee or payment status records.</li>
                    <li>Ratings and feedback you submit, and an optional profile photo if you choose to upload one.</li>
                    <li>Session and browser storage needed for sign-in, security, and interface preferences.</li>
                </ul>

                <h3>How information is used</h3>
                <p>Information is used to create and secure accounts, verify email addresses, operate queues, display ticket and service information, maintain payment and feedback records, and provide service support.</p>

                <h3>When information is shared</h3>
                <p>Authorized Queuezy administrators and participating staff may access information needed to operate the service. Information may also be processed by infrastructure or email providers used to host the service, store its database, or deliver verification messages. Information may be disclosed when required by law or to protect the service and its users.</p>

                <h3>Payments</h3>
                <p>Queuezy records service amounts and payment status. Do not enter payment-card details into Queuezy unless a specific payment screen expressly requests them. If a separate payment provider is used, its privacy policy applies to information you provide directly to that provider.</p>

                <h3>Retention and your choices</h3>
                <p>Information is retained as needed to operate accounts and queues and to maintain service, security, and financial records. You may ask the Queuezy administrator to review, correct, or delete account information. Some records may need to remain where required for legitimate operational or legal purposes.</p>

                <h3>Security and policy updates</h3>
                <p>Queuezy uses safeguards such as password hashing and access controls. No internet service can guarantee absolute security. This policy may be updated as Queuezy changes; the date above indicates when it was last revised.</p>
            </section>
        </main>
    </div>
</body>
</html>